Declare rules_oci's repo rules reproducible so they can use the repo contents cache, and keep host
credentials out of the cache key of digest pulls.

Bazel refuses to store a repo in the repo contents cache unless its implementation returns
`repo_metadata(reproducible = True)`. Without this every `bazel clean --expunge`, and every
cache miss on a fresh checkout, refetches crane, regctl, cosign and each pulled image layer.

Even then, a digest-pinned `oci_pull`/`oci_alias` recorded `~/.docker/config.json` as an input
(`rctx.read` with the default `watch = "auto"`) and declared `HOME` and friends in `environ`, so
CI's per-run `GITHUB_TOKEN` login meant it never hit the cache. Digest pulls now read the
credential file with `watch = "no"` and declare no `environ`; tag pulls still watch both. The
credential-helper and OAuth2 shim scripts are also deleted after running.

Carries all three commits of the upstream PR, a215a05, 59c69f2 and 3888554, onto 2.3.0. The last
conflicted in `_fetch_auth_via_creds_helper` with an unrelated upstream change to its
`rctx.execute(...)` call; 2.3.0's call is kept.

Upstream fix: https://github.com/bazel-contrib/rules_oci/pull/901
Drop this patch, and the `single_version_override` pinning it, once that lands in a release.

